The potential vulnerability is related to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application processes user-supplied regex patterns without adequate validation or restrictions, allowing an attacker to craft complex regex patterns that can cause excessive backtracking. This can lead to significant performance degradation or even application crashes, as the regex engine may take an inordinate amount of time to evaluate these patterns, especially when they are applied to large datasets or files. The lack of constraints on the regex input can thus expose the application to denial-of-service attacks, impacting its availability and responsiveness.

